      ":question/math-academy-id": "e-14365",
      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the line that is perpendicular to $x=2$ and passes through the point $(3,4).$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since the line $x=2$ is a vertical line, a perpendicular line would need to be horizontal. So, the perpendicular line must take the form $y=k$ for some value of $k.$\n\nThe perpendicular line needs to go through the point $(3,4),$ which has a $y$-coordinate of $4.$ So, the perpendicular line is $y=4.$"
    },
